  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: Severe \"blinding\" headache for 3 days.\n- Symptoms: Sudden onset on waking 3 days ago; continuous headache that is partially relieved by ibuprofen (from ~8/10 to ~5/10). Pain generalized but stronger over right eye. Photophobia and intermittent \"shooting lights\"/visual phenomena. Feels a bit sick but no vomiting. No sensory loss, weakness, or change in smell/taste. Not worse at night and does not wake her from sleep. Occasionally a stabbing pain when standing up quickly or moving the head. No cough-induced or position-related worsening clearly reported. Sleeps okay.\n- Past medical history: Occasional past headaches (mild, short-lived). No other chronic illnesses reported.\n- Medications / allergies: Combined oral contraceptive pill started ~1 year ago. Uses ibuprofen intermittently for headaches. No allergies reported.\n- Family / social history: Mother has severe migraines (with vomiting). Lives alone. Non-smoker. Drinks alcohol approximately once weekly (\"three, once a week\"). No recreational drug use reported.\n- Vital signs / exam findings: None recorded in transcript; clinician planned neurological exam and fundoscopy. Patient reports pharmacy BP check ~1 year ago was normal.\n- Labs / imaging: None performed or reported in the transcript.",
